{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1355179-generic-artifact-special-features","id":1355179,"title":"Generic artifact special features","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-16T07:26:21-08:00","id":1355179,"title":"Generic artifact special features","content":"So... a thing that has been bothering me for a while - and to a certain extent it's been addressed with the advent of evocations, but that doesn't cover 2nd edition which I will still cling to quite comfortably until I hear of 3rd ed alchies.<br /> <br /> Anywho:<br /> <br /> Say you pick a 2-dot daiklaive. Neat. The lore has it that even such an artifact has a story, has a name, is special... but its &quot;just&quot; a 2-dot daiklaive.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of introducing a rule to future games I ST, that &quot;generic&quot; artifacts come with at least one special feature - nothing gamebreaking, ideally just utility features, but none the less something to make them slightly less generic.<br /> <br /> <br /> My inspiration is stuff like the red jade daiklave that the bull of the north has, which can light things on fire at a tough at the cost of 2m. That's the kind of basic utility features I'm thinking. Like, an orichalcum daiklaive or suit of armor being able to light up for a scene with the brightness of a torch for 2m. It's nothing grand, but handy.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T07:36:18-08:00","id":1355181,"title":"","content":"You might want to check out 3e\u2019s attunement bonuses for some inspiration. Not only do 3e artifacts have evocations, but all of them have a unique ability that activates upon attuning to it. For example the white jade tetsubo Faith\u2019s Pillar lets you pick a religious belief upon attuning to it and get +1 to your resolve against influence that opposes it, or the orichalcum chakram Sunflash, which possesses it\u2019s own Solar anima that increases as it fights and improves the attacks with every level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T17:16:47-08:00","id":1355294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1355179-generic-artifact-special-features?p=1355181#post1355181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to check out 3e\u2019s attunement bonuses for some inspiration. Not only do 3e artifacts have evocations, but all of them have a unique ability that activates upon attuning to it. For example the white jade tetsubo Faith\u2019s Pillar lets you pick a religious belief upon attuning to it and get +1 to your resolve against influence that opposes it, or the orichalcum chakram Sunflash, which possesses it\u2019s own Solar anima that increases as it fights and improves the attacks with every level.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair nuf - though as I was saying: I don't want stuff that actually has &quot;useful&quot; effects. Only simple utility stuff. But still, not a bad idea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T21:13:07-08:00","id":1355335,"title":"","content":"Saying you don't want it to be useful, just to have utility, is kind of a hard river to bridge there, what with the words meaning the same thing. I imagine though that the main concern is you don't want them to be powerful enough to basically be incorporating another one dot artifact for free, and that you probably want to avoid combat oriented effects. <br /> <br /> Looking at some one dot effects, +1m per hour, +3 dice on a check, keep you clean for 1m, never run out of ink, it seems to me like either one dot specialty in one of the abilities, and a relevant shape to boot would good, (if you make sure it can't break the no more than three specialty dice cap rule I think it's fine to be combat related) or replace the heartstone socket with another one dot effect. Since a hearthstone amulet is a one dot artifact, that seems like it would be about right, and allow you to make the sword a lot scarier in some respects, if it gives you a +3 on certain check or other such effects. I do like the idea of each one being unique, although the whole factory cathedral set up for mass producing artifacts makes me think maybe not all of them *are* unique. Another way to do it would be to stat up a least god with a unique personality that can regale you with tales of the first age, maybe even act as a tutor for melee, but can also block attunement if it finds you wanting. I don't know how strictly that last part sticks to RAW though, since sapient artifacts have their whole own thing going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","user":"Santova","date":".  Spelling error 12-17-2019, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25854-santova","name":"Santova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T03:16:44-08:00","id":1355353,"title":"","content":"Add a piece of mundane equipment to the weapon/armour i.e. moonsilver baneclaw might be a perfect lockpick. You could also make the equipment a secondary weapon like a red jade daiklave might incorporate a firewand.<br /> <br /> It basically works for 3rd edition too except that an artifact's attunement bonus can be expected to outperform the +1 dice from superior equipment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-17-2019, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T04:05:49-08:00","id":1355360,"title":"","content":"Another way to handle it would be to copy stuff from Hearthstones and give any generic Artifact a bonus that's equivalent to a Hearthstone that's worth half the Artifacts rating.<br /> <br /> This will keep it away from the more potent ones, but gives a lot of options for minor effects. And for characters that can't easily maintain lots of Manses, it makes some of those effects more accessible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T12:30:26-08:00","id":1355464,"title":"","content":"exactly<br /> <br /> 1dot hearthstone effects are IMO great examples of the kind of things I'm looking for, though ideally it shouldn't give any stat or ability bonuses that make getting the real deal unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}